hadiths[127]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3409","(Stopped hadith) Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Asim, from Abu al-Ahwaz, from Abdullah, that he said: \Indeed"," everything has a peak"," and the peak of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah. And indeed"," everything has its purest essence"," and the purest essence of the Quran is the Mufassal.\"" Abu Muhammad said: \""Al-Lubab means the purest part.\"""""
"3410","Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad said: Whoever recites Surah Baqarah, he will be crowned in Paradise."
"3411","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Mas'ud Radiyallahu Anhu said: When Satan hears Surah Baqarah being recited in a house, he runs away from that house."
"3412","Ifa bin Abdullah al-Kala'i said: A Companion said: O Messenger of Allah! Which Surah of the Holy Quran is the greatest? He said: \Qul hu Allah is the greatest.\"" He said: And whose verse is the greatest? He said: \""Ayat al-Kursi:\"" \""There is no god but He"," the Living"," the Everlasting.\"" . . . . .﴾» [Al-Baqarah: 255/2]"," then he said: O Prophet of Allah! Which is the verse that you like and which is beneficial for you and your Ummah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The last verses of Surah Al-Baqarah are among the treasures of Allah's mercy under the Throne"," which Allah has bestowed especially on this Ummah"," which include all the goodness and goodness of this world and the Hereafter.\"""""
"3413","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) said: A man from among the companions of Muhammad (PBUH) met one of the jinn and wrestled with him, and this man overthrew the jinn and said: Do you look weak and tired to me? Your wrists are like the wrists of a dog, so are all the jinn like that or are you the only one among them? He replied: By Allah! I am the one with the strongest bones among the jinn, you wrestle with me again, if you knock me down again, I will tell you something that will benefit you. This Companion said: Well, come, then he knocked the jinn down again and said: Now tell me that thing, did you say: «﴿Allah la ilaha illa huwa al-hayyūp al-Qayyoom. . . . . Do you read (Ayat al-Kursi)? He said: Yes, I recite it. The Jinn said: In whatever house you recite it, the devil will leave it defecating like a donkey, then the devil will not enter that house until morning. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: \Al-Zhiyal\"" means weak and thin and \""Al-Shakhit\"": tired"," \""Al-Zali'\"" means good and strong ribs and \""Al-Khabj\"" means air."""
"3414","It is narrated from Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: Whoever recites ten verses of Surah Al-Baqarah at night, the devil will not enter his house that night until morning. . . . . .﴾» starts with"
"3415","On the authority of Shaabi, may God have mercy on him, Sayyiduna Ibn Mas’ud, may God be pleased with him, said: “Whoever recites the first four verses of Surah Baqarah, and Ayat al-Kursi, and the two verses after that, and the last three verses, on that day Shaytan will not come near him or his family, nor will there be anything that he dislikes, and if these verses are recited even to a madman, he will become insane.”"
"3416","Abu Ishaq narrated from the person who heard from Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: I do not think that any man who is wise can go to sleep after reciting the last verse of Surah Al-Baqarah, these verses belong to the treasure under the Throne."
"3417","Mugheera bin Sabi, who was among the students of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, said: A person who recites ten verses of Surah Baqarah while sleeping will not forget the Holy Qur'an. Those verses are: the beginning four verses, the Ayat al-Kursi and the two verses after it, and the last three verses. Isaac said: He will not forget what he has memorized. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Some have called the narrator Mughirah bin Sami."
"3418","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: “Whoever recites Ayat al-Kursi, Ham (Surah Al-Mu’min) from the beginning to “﴿"
"3419","On the authority of Sayyidna Nu'man bin Basheer, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Allah wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth"," and sent down two verses from it"," with which he concluded Surah Al-Baqarah (i.e."," the last two verses)"," and these two verses are recited for three nights in the house from which Satan will not come near.\"""""
"3420","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Mas'ud Ansari, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah Al-Baqarah"," they are sufficient for him.\"" It is in Sahih Bukhari: \""Whoever recites the last two verses of Surah Baqarah at night"," they will be sufficient for him (to save him from every calamity).\"""""
"3421","Sayyida Asma bint Yazid, may God be pleased with her, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The Greatest Name of Allah is in these two verses: “There is no god but Allah, the Living, the Living.” [Al-Baqarah: 255/2] ﴿"
"3422","It was narrated on the authority of Jubayr bin Nafir that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Indeed"," Allah has finished Surah Baqarah with two verses which have been given to me from the treasure under the Throne. You should learn them and teach them to your wives"," for these two verses are blessings"," the Qur'an"," and supplication.\"""""
"3423","Abdullah bin Burida narrated from his father, he said: I was sitting with the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I heard him saying: \Learn Surah Al-Baqarah"," its acquisition (i.e. reading) is a blessing and its abandonment is regret"," and magicians cannot resist it.\"" will cast shadows on its reciter as if there are two clouds or canopies"," or two flocks of birds in flight"," these two surahs will be defended by their reciters"," and the Holy Qur'an will come to its reciter on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a tired person (whose color has changed due to illness and travel) and the Qur'an will say to him: Do you know me? He will answer: No. The Qur'an will say: I am the Qur'an"," your companion"," who kept you thirsty in the summer afternoon (i.e. kept reciting the Qur'an even when thirsty)"," woke you up at night"," while every merchant was engaged in his trade"," but today you are behind every kind of trade. Those two parents will say: Why have these clothes been put on us? They will be answered: It is because of your son's memorization of the Qur'an"," then it will be said to him (the Qur'an memorizer): Go read the Qur'an and climb the ladder of heaven"," so he will continue to climb as long as he recites it."""
"3424","Abu Yahya narrated on the authority of Salim bin Amir, he heard from Abu Umamah, he used to say: One of your brothers saw in a dream that people were walking in a long and terrifying crevasse of a mountain, and on the top of the mountain there were two green trees that were making a sound: Is there anyone among you who recites Surah Al-Baqarah? Is there anyone among you who recites Surah Aal Imran? So, if a man answers in the affirmative, those two trees close their branches for him, and by holding them, that person reaches the top of the mountain. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: They are called the stems and branches."
"3425","It is narrated from Masrooq that a man recited Surah Baqarah and Aal Imran to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: You have recited two such surahs in which the Name of Allah is the Greatest, that if you pray with this name, it will be accepted, and if you ask for anything, it will be granted."
"3426","On the authority of Abu Ataf, Sayyiduna Ka'b al-Ahbar, may God be pleased with him, said: Whoever recites Surah Baqarah and Aal Imran, these two surahs will come on the Day of Judgment and request Allah Almighty: O our Lord! Don't put him in trouble."
"3427","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: He who recites Aal Imran is rich and (for him) women are beautiful. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: «Mahbara»: Muzeena means decorated with ornaments."
"3428","Sayyiduna Uthman bin Affan (RA) said: Whoever recites the last verses of Surah Aal-Imran at night, the reward of staying up all night will be recorded for him."
"3429","Makhool (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Whoever recites Surah Al-Imran on Friday, the angels pray for him till night."
"3430","Abdullah said: Jabir narrated to me, before he fell into misrepresentation, that Sha'bi, may God have mercy on him, said: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, said: How good is the treasure of those poor people, Surah Al-Imran, which they recite in the last part of the night."
"3431","Abul Salil said: A man was obliged to die (retribution), he said: I go to the Valley of the Jinn and take refuge, and it was such a valley that anyone who went there would be jinn, and there were two monks on the edge of that valley. A good surah has been recited, perhaps he will be saved, the narrator said: So the morning came and he was in good health. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The name of Abul Salil is al-Qaif bin Faqir and he is called Ibn Nafir."
"3432","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him) said: The first seven long chapters of the Qur'an are like the Torah, and the chapters with two hundred verses are like the Gospel, and the remaining chapters are like the Psalms, and after that the whole Qur'an is more than these heavenly books."
"3433","On the authority of Abdullah bin Khalifa, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Surah Al-An'am is obligatory from the Qur'an."
"3434","On the authority of Abdullah Ibn Rabah, Sayyiduna Ka'b al-Ahbar (RA) said: The first Surah of the Torah is Surah Inam and the last Surah is Hud."
"3435","Abdullah bin Rabah said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Recite Surah Hud on Friday.\"""""
"3436","On the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, Sayyiduna Ka'b (may God be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Recite Hud on Friday.\"""""
"3437","Khalid bin Madan said: Whoever recites the last ten verses of Surah Kahf, he will not fear Dajjal."
"3438","Zar bin Habish said: Whoever recites the last ten verses of Surah Kahf at some point in order to stay up during the night, he will get up (at that time). Abdu said: We tested it and found it to be so."
"3439","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: Whoever recites Surah Kahf on the night of Friday, there is light for him from it to the House of Allah."
"3440","Khalid bin Madan said: Recite the sura of deliverance, I have heard that a man used to recite it, he did not recite anything other than it, he was very sinful, this surah spread its wings over that person and asked Allah Almighty: O Lord! This man used to recite me frequently, so Allah Ta'ala accepted his intercession and said: Write one good deed for each of his mistakes and raise him one level (in some manuscripts, after Manjiyyah, there is \alm tanzil al-sajda\"". That is"," this Surah is a savior."""
"3441","On the authority of Abdullah bin Zamra, Sayyiduna Ka'b al-Ahbar (may God be pleased with him) said: Whoever recites \Tanzir al-Sajda\"" and \""Tabarak al-Baida al-Malik\"" 70 good deeds will be recorded for him and seventy sins will be erased and seventy degrees will be raised for him."""
"3442","Khalid bin Ma'dan said: Surely (Surah Al-Tanzil) will argue for its reciter in the grave, she will say: O Allah! If I am from Your Book (Quran), then accept my intercession regarding it, and if I am not from Your Book, then erase me from it, and it will be like a bird that overshadows it, it will intercede for it (the reciter) and save it from the punishment of the grave, and (Surah) «Tabarak» is like that. Therefore, Khalid bin Madan himself did not sleep after reading these two surahs."
"3443","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not sleep until he had recited “Alm al-Sajda” and “Tabarak”."
"3444","Taaws, may Allah have mercy on him, said: These two surahs of the Qur'an (\Sajdah\"" and \""Tabarak\"") are sixty virtues (degrees) higher than each surah."""
"3445","On the authority of Amr bin Marawi, he heard from his father Mara, he used to say: A man was buried in his grave, when punishment came to his grave, then a Surah with thirty verses came and defended him. The narrator said: Me and Masrooq have considered, then we do not find thirty verses in any other surah except «Tabarak»."
"3446","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Allah the Exalted and Exalted recited Ta and Yas a thousand years before He created the earth and the heavens"," and when the angels heard the Holy Qur'an"," they said: Enviable is the nation on which these Surahs were revealed"," and enviable are the hearts in which these Surahs reside"," and enviable are the tongues on which they are recited.\"""""
"3447","Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Whoever recites Surah Yes at night for the pleasure of Allah, he will be forgiven. He said: I was informed that this Surah is equal to the entire Qur'an."
"3448","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Everything has a heart"," and the heart of the Qur'an (Sura) is Yes"," and whoever recites it"," it is as if he had recited the Holy Qur'an ten times.\"""""
"3449","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever recites Surah Yas at night seeking the pleasure of Allah"," will be forgiven in that night.\"""""
"3450","Ata bin Abi Rabah said: I have been informed that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites Surah Yes at the beginning of the day"," all his needs will be fulfilled.\"""""
"3451","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever recites Surah Yas in the morning will be eased for him until evening, and whoever recites it at the beginning of the night will be eased until dawn."
"3452","Abdullah bin Isa said: I have been informed that whoever recites Surah Dukhan on Friday night with faith and conviction, he will be forgiven if he wakes up in the morning."
"3453","Abu Rafi' said: Whoever recites Surah Dukhan on Friday night is forgiven, and he is married to Hurayn."
"3454","Sa'd bin Ibrahim said: The Surahs beginning with Ham were called Dulhan."
"3455","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: Whoever recites the last three verses of Surah Al-Hashr and dies on the same day, the seal of the martyrs will be placed on him, and if he recites it in the evening and dies at night, he will still be counted among the martyrs."
"3456","Khalid bin Ma'dan said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite the Musabat (i.e. the surahs that start with \Subh"," Yasbah\"") while sleeping and used to say: \""There is one verse in it that is equal to a thousand verses.\"""""
"3457","On the authority of Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever recites the last three verses of Surah Al-Hashr in the morning after “Awz bilallah al-Sami’ al-Aleem min al-Shaytaan al-Arjim”, Allah will appoint seventy thousand angels for him who pray for forgiveness for him until the evening, and if he recites it in the evening, they pray for him in the same way until the morning.”"
"3458","Abul Hasan Muhajar said: During the time of Ziyad, a Companion came to Kufa, I heard him, he was narrating the Hadith that I was on the way with the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my knee was touching the blessed knee of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \This person has been absolved from polytheism.\"" He heard another person reciting \""Qul Hu Allah Ahad\"" and said: \""He has been forgiven.\"""""
"3459","Farah bin Nawfal narrated from his father (Sayyidna Nawfal, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said (to him): What brought you (to me)? He said: I have come so that you may remind me of something that I should recite while sleeping. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When you lie down on the bed"," recite \""Qul ya ayyah al-kafiroon\"" and go to sleep at the end of it"," because it is an absolution from shirk.\"" (That is"," it is absolving from Shirk)."""
"3460","Nouf bin Fazallah Bakali said: Verily, Allah Ta'ala divided the Holy Qur'an into three parts and called \Qul Hu Allah Ahad\"" as one third."""
"3461","Abu Aqeel reported that he heard from Saeed bin Al-Musayb, may God have mercy on him, that he used to say: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever recites the Surah Al-Ikhlas ten times, a palace will be built for him in Paradise, and whoever recites it twenty times, two palaces will be built for him, and whoever recites it thirty times, three palaces will be built for him.” The palace will be in Paradise\"," Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu said: Then"," O Messenger of Allah"," we will build many palaces. The Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: \""Verily"," Allah is the Most Expanding.\"" Abu Muhammad Imam al-Darmi"," may God have mercy on him"," said: Abu Aqeel's name is Zahra bin Mabad"," and he was said to be one of the abdals."""
"3462","Uqbah bin Zamra bin Habib narrated from his father that whenever he finished reciting a surah, he used to recite “Qul Huwa Allah Ahad” after it."
"3463","Sayyiduna Abu Darda said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Isn't one of you capable of reciting a third of the Qur'an in one night?\"" The Companions said: We are unable and weak to read so much of the Qur’an in one night. are)."""
"3464","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu used to say: \Qul huwa Allah is one person\"" (Surah Al-Ikhlas) is equal to a third of the Qur'an."""
"3465","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: \Qul hu wa Allah is ahad\"" is equal to a third of the Qur'an."""
"3466","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated the same."
"3467","On the authority of Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, a Companion said: By Allah, I love this Surah \Qul Hu Allah Ahad\"" very much. The Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: \""Your love (of this Surah) has made you enter Paradise.\"""""
"3468","Hameed bin Abd al-Rahman narrated from his father that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about \Qul Hu Allah Ahad\"" and he"," may Allah bless him and grant him peace"," said: \""Third is the Qur'an\"" or \""Third is equal to the Qur'an.\"""""
"3469","On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, he narrated from a woman of the Ansar that Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) came to her and said: Do you know what the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) brought? This female Ansari Sahabi replied: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, has come to us with many good things. Tell me, what news has he brought? Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: \Is there anyone among you who is unable to recite a third of the Qur'an in one night?\"" We were afraid that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted us to do something that we did not have the power to do"," so we did not answer. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) repeated this question three times and said: \""Isn't one of you strong enough to recite Surah Ikhlas?\"""""
"3470","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Whoever recites \""Qul Hu Allah Ahad\"" fifty times"," his sins of fifty years will be forgiven."""
"3471","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I held the blessed feet of the Messenger of Allah (may God bless him and grant him peace) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Recite Surah Hud and Surah Yusuf to me. The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: \O Uqbah! You will never recite any surah of the Qur'an that is more beloved and eloquent to Allah than \""Qul a'Udhu birabbi al-Falaq\"" (that is"," Surah Al-Falaq is the most beloved and eloquent to Allah).\"" Yazid said: Abu Imran used to recite it in Maghrib prayer."""
"3472","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: I was walking with the Holy Prophet (SAW) when he said: \O Uqbah! Say.\"" I said: \""What shall I say?\"" Sayyiduna Uqbah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: He became silent"," then after some time he said: \""O Uqbah! Say\"""," I again asked: What should I say? He said: \""Qul-a-Udzu birabbi al-falaq\"""," so I read the entire Surah till the end"," then the Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: \""No one who asked sought refuge like him"," and no one who sought refuge sought refuge like him.\"""""
"3473","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Aamir (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Some verses have been revealed to me"," the likes of which have not been seen"," namely"," ``Say"," ``I seek refuge with the Lord of the heavens'' and ``Say"," ``I seek refuge with the Lord of the People.''\"""""
"3474","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The person who recites ten verses in a night will not be listed among the negligent."
"3475","On the authority of Sayyidna Tamim Dari and Sayyidna Fazla bin Ubayd (may Allah be pleased with them): Whoever recites ten verses (of the Qur'an) in a night, (his name) will be written among those who pray."
"3476","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: He who recites ten verses at night will not be listed among the heedless."
"3477","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever recites ten verses at night will not be listed among the heedless."
"3478","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Whoever recites fifty verses in a night will not be listed among the heedless."
"3479","Sayyidna Tamim Dari and Sayyidna Fazala bin Ubayd (may Allah be pleased with them) said: Whoever recites fifty verses in one night will be written in Hafaz."
"3480","On the authority of Sayyidina Abul-Darda, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites a hundred verses in one night"," he will not be listed among the negligent.\"" Imam Darmi"," may God have mercy on him"," said: Some narrators have mentioned the name of Rashid bin Saad instead of \""Salam\""."""
"3481","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever recites a hundred verses in one night, it will be written in the Qur'an."
"3482","On the authority of Sayyiduna Tamim Dari, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites a hundred verses in one night"," one night of Qunoot will be written for him.\"""""
"3483","Sayyiduna Ka'b al-Ahbar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever recites a hundred verses, he is recorded in the qantin (obedient ones)."
"3484","Both Sayyidna Tamim Dari and Sayyidna Fazala bin Ubayd (RA) said: Whoever recites a hundred verses at night, it is written down in Qantin."
"3485","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu said: Whoever recites a hundred verses in the night, it is written down in Qantin."
"3486","Habib bin Ubayd said: I heard from Sayyidina Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: He who recites a hundred verses will not be written among the heedless."
"3487","Habib bin Ubaid said: I heard from Sayyidina Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: Whoever recites two hundred verses, it will be written in Qantin."
"3488","On the authority of Sayyidina Abu Darda, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \Whoever recites two hundred verses in the night"," he is written among the obedient.\"""""
"3489","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Whoever recites ten verses at night will not be listed among the negligent, and whoever recites a hundred verses will be listed among the Qantin, and whoever recites two hundred verses will be listed among the Faizeen. (That is, he will be counted among the successful people)."
"3490","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, said: He who recites ten verses at night will be written among those who remember Allah, and he who recites a hundred verses will be written among those who are obedient and obedient, and he who recites from five hundred to a thousand verses will wake up in the morning with a quintal of reward. He was asked: How much is a row? So they said: As much as gold stuffed in the skin of an ox."
"3491","It was narrated from Hasan, may God have mercy on him, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites a hundred verses at night"," the Holy Qur'an will not argue against him that night"," and whoever recites two hundred verses at night"," a whole night of prayer and remembrance is written for him"," and whoever recites from five hundred to a thousand verses"," there will be a quintar for him in the Hereafter.\"" People asked: What is a quintar? Said: \""Twelve thousand (good deeds).\"""""
"3492","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: One quintar (of reward) was written for the person who recited three hundred verses in the night, and whoever recited seven hundred verses, I do not know what they said about him."
"3493","Habib bin Ubaid said: I heard from Sayyidina Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to say: Whoever recites a thousand verses, a quintal of reward and reward is written for him, and that kirat is greater than your kirat of this world, that is: there can be no comparison or equality with the kirat of this world."
"3494","Both Sayyidna Tamim Dari and Sayyidna Fazala bin Ubaid (RA) said: A quintal (reward) has been written for a person who recites a thousand verses in one night, and the weight of this quintal is better than the quintal of the world and all that is in it."
"3495","It was narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Abul-Dardaa, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever recites a thousand verses"," a quintal of reward is written for him"," whose karat is equal to a huge mound.\"""""
"3496","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him: A quintar is twelve thousand."
"3497","Abu Nazrah al-Abdi said: A quintal is equal to the skin of an ox filled with gold."
"3498","Saeed bin Al-Masib, may God have mercy on him, said: A quintar is forty thousand."
"3499","Hasan, may God have mercy on him, said: According to one of you, the quintar is twelve thousand."
"3500","On the authority of Mujahid, may God have mercy on him, he said: A quintar is seventy thousand."
"3501","Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him, said: A quintar is twelve thousand ounces."
"3502","Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: (Quantar) is seventy thousand shekels."
"3503","Abu Qalaba narrated that the person who was present at the beginning (opening) of the Holy Qur'an is as if he was present at the victory of the way of Allah, and the one who was present at the end of the Qur'an is as if he was present at the distribution of spoils."
"3504","Qatadah, may God have mercy on him, said: A man was reciting in the mosque of Madinah, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) made a man wait for him. (In other words, he came to this reciter to join the Khatam Qur'an, he learned the virtue of attending the Khatam Qur'an.)"
"3505","When Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) would get close to finishing the Qur'an, he would leave a little bit of the Qur'an until dawn, then he would gather his family members and finish the Qur'an with them."
"3506","Thabit al-Banani said: When Sayyiduna Anas (RA) finished the Holy Qur'an, he would gather his children and family members and pray for everyone."
"3507","Abdah said: When a person finishes reciting the Holy Qur'an during the day, the angels pray for him until the evening, and when he finishes reciting it at night, the angels pray for him until the morning."
"3508","It was narrated from Zarara bin Abi Awfi that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked: Which deed is best? He said: \To teach and to coach\"". It was asked: What is this? He said: \""A person who recites the Qur'an reads from the beginning to the end (this is to begin)"," then to finish it is to start again (arthal). Whenever he finishes"," he should start again.\"""""
"3509","Ibrahim al-Nakh'i, may God have mercy on him, said: When a person recites the Qur'an at the beginning of the day, the angels pray for him until the evening, and if he recites (i.e. finished) at night, the angels pray for him until the morning. (Aamish) Sulaiman said: That is why we saw our contemporary companions that they liked to finish the Qur'an at the beginning of the day and at the beginning of the night."
"3510","From this chain, Ibrahim Nakhai, may God have mercy on him, narrated the same as before, but it does not contain the words of Sulaiman al-Aamish."
"3511","Mohareb bin Dasar, may God have mercy on him, said: Whoever recites the Qur'an by mouth, there is a call for him in this world and in the Hereafter."
"3512","Both Talha and Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Aswad said: Whoever recites the Holy Qur'an at night or during the day, the angels pray for him until the night. The other said: He is forgiven."
"3513","Hameed al-Araj, may Allah have mercy on him, said: \Whoever recites the Holy Qur'an and prays"," four thousand angels will say Amen to his prayer.\"""""
"3514","Mujahid, may Allah have mercy on him, said: A call came to me and said, \We invite you to participate in the recitation of the Qur'an"," because we have heard that dua is accepted during the recitation of the Qur'an"," and he prayed.\"""""
"3515","Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may God be pleased with him) said: If the end of the Qur'an is finished in the early part of the night, then the angels pray for him (the reciter) until dawn, and if the end of the night is agreed upon, then the angels pray for him until the evening. Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith is good from Sayyidna Saad (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"3516","Ata bin Yasar, may God have mercy on him, said: Those who have the Qur'an will be the Naqeeb (monitors) in Paradise."
"3517","Abdul Malik reported that Saeed bin Jubayr, may God have mercy on him, used to finish the Holy Quran every second night."
"3518","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas (RA) said: I said: O Messenger of Allah! In how many days should I finish the Holy Quran? He said: \In one month\"""," I said: Do I have more power than that? He said: \""Finish it in twenty-five days.\"" I said: I have more power than that. He said: \""Finish it in fifteen days.\"" I said: I have more power than that. He said: \""Finish it in ten days.\"" I said: I have more power than that. He said: \""Finish it in five days.\"""""
"3519","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade me to finish the Holy Qur'an in less than three days."
"3520","On the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \He who does not recite the Qur'an with pleasure is not one of us.\"" Ibn Ayaina said: \""Lim Yatgun\"" means \""Yistghani\"". Abu Muhammad Imam Darmi"," may God have mercy on him"," said: People call Abu Naheek Ubaidullah bin Abi Naheek."""
"3521","On the authority of Taus, may Allah have mercy on him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked: Which person has a good voice for the Qur'an? Or who is a good reciter? He said: \When you hear him reciting"," it seems that he is afraid of Allah.\"" Taus"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Talaq was like that."""
"3522","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) said: \Allah did not listen to anything as attentively as He listened to His Prophet Muhammad (PBUH) reciting the Qur'an with the best voice.\"" Abu Salama's disciple said: He meant to recite the Qur'an aloud."""
"3523","This document also states the same as mentioned above."
"3524","Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman reported that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say about Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, who used to recite the Qur'an with a very good voice: \He has been given the best voice like that of David.\"""""
"3525","It was Abu Salama who narrated that Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) whenever he saw Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA), he used to say: O Abu Musa! Remembrance of our Lord, so he would recite the Qur'an to them."
"3526","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I will not find any of you reciting the Qur'an with one foot on top of another and omitting Surah Baqarah. Verily, the devil flees from a house in which Surah Baqarah is recited, and indeed desolate houses are those in which the Book of God is not recited."
"3527","Someone from the family of Salim bin Abdullah, may Allah have mercy on him, said: When Salim al-Bizq came to Medina and began to lead the prayer, Salim, may God have mercy on him, was asked: I wish you would also go and listen to his recitation. So when Salim bin Abdullah reached the door and heard his recitation, he returned and said: Singing is singing."
"3528","Ibn Shihab Al-Zuhari, may God have mercy on him, narrated on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abd al-Rahman, that when Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) used to visit Sayyidna Umar (RA), Ameerul Momineen would say to him: Remember our Lord, so he used to recite to him."
"3529","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Allah has not permitted anyone like a prophet (Muhammad himself) to recite the Qur'an with a melodious voice\"""," that is"," He has permitted the reading of the Qur'an aloud."""
"3530","Abdullah bin Burida narrated from his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Sayyidna Abu Musa"," may Allah be pleased with him"," has been given the melodious voice of the House of Dawud.\"""""
"3531","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: When the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) came, he heard the recitations of a companion, and he said: \Who are these?\"" It was narrated: Abdullah bin Qays (Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari"," may God be pleased with him) said: \""He has been given a (melodious) voice in the psalms of the House of Dawud.\"""""
"3532","On the authority of Sayyidina Bara bin Azib, the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \Adorn the Qur'an with your voice.\"""""
"3533","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (PBUH) saying: \Recite the Qur'an in your good voice"," for a good voice makes the Qur'an more pleasing.\"""""
"3534","Amish (Sulaiman bin Mehran may Allah have mercy on him) said: A man recited in front of Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) and he was reciting aloud, which Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) disliked. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The second narrator said: Ghorak bin Abi al-Khidram recited it."
"3535","Muhammad bin Sirin, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The predecessors used to consider these chapters as innovation in the recitation of the Qur'an."
